  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1...Multiple rounds of showers and thunderstorms \nare expected tonight through Wednesday, with heavy downpours and\nlocalized gusty winds.\n\nSurface analysis shows low pressure over northern Wisconsin with a \nwarm front extending south into the Ohio Valley this afternoon. Deep \nconvection exists near Lake Michigan and Lake Huron. Closer to home, \nridging remains across the Northeast with light winds aloft. Daytime \nheating and dewpoints in the mid 60s will support diurnally driven \nshowers and thunderstorms across the terrain and inland from the \nlakes this afternoon.\n\nThe surface low is expected to move across the central Great Lakes \ntonight. A corridor of increasing mid-level winds, steepening mid-\nlevel lapse rates, and high PWATS will move into the Ohio Valley and \nparts of western NY late tonight. Mean 0-6km wind shear will \nincrease to 20-30 knots across far western NY, remaining less than \n20 knots east of the Genesee Valley. The storm motion of the ongoing \norganized convection across the Central Great Lakes is expected to \nmove south, and stay west of the forecast area, however additional \nshowers and thunderstorms are expected to develop as the surface low \napproaches the region tonight. Numerous showers and thunderstorms \nare expected to move across western NY through Tuesday morning. \nConditions are marginally favorable for an isolated severe \nthunderstorm across far western NY tonight, with gusty winds and \nheavy rain as the main hazards. \n\nThe surface low is expected to track across western NY Tuesday, then \nbecome nearly stationary across north-central NY Tuesday night \nthrough Wednesday. Showers will taper off across far western NY \nTuesday morning. Diurnal heating within a very moist environment \nwill support additional showers and thunderstorms during peak \nheating. A low level jet will wrap around the low and a few strong \nthunderstorms with heavy rainfall may lead to localized flooding \nacross parts of the Finger Lakes region and north-central NY Tuesday \nafternoon through Tuesday night. As the low spins across northern \nNew York Tuesday night, wrap around moisture will support chances \nfor showers across western NY overnight. There is a Marginal Risk of \nExcessive Rainfall for portions of western and north-central \nNY through Wednesday.\n\nExpect a cool Wednesday, with highs in the low to mid 70s, 60s \nacross the higher terrain.\n\nKey Message 2...Chances for showers and thunderstorms are expected \nto linger into Thursday, with drier conditions for the end of the \nwork week.\n\nThe anomalously strong low will move off the southern New England \ncoast Thursday. While moisture is expected to pull away from the \nforecast area, diurnally driven convection remains possible, \nespecially across interior locations. Expect another cool day with \nhighs in the 70s. \n\nHigh pressure will move into the eastern Great Lakes region for the \nend of the week bringing dry and seasonal weather.",
